%% Note X1: <b>guards.profile</b> (off | standard | strict) is read in EACH layer separately: crew_guards.layer_guard_state :638 looks up the
%%    layer's profile in PROFILE_MAP :240. off is today's GUARD_DEFAULTS, so a layer that sets nothing resolves as it always did.
%%    The profile itself is never ratcheted.
%% Note X2: <b>guards.overrides.&lt;guard&gt;</b> in the same layer replaces the profile's value for that one guard, validated against
%%    that guard's own tiers. An override can never widen past a malformed profile or past a legacy key still present.
%% Note X3: <b>The twelve legacy guards.&lt;name&gt; keys</b> are still READ as aliases until /crew:migrate rewrites the layer, and never
%%    written. When a legacy key and a profile or override both speak, the NARROWER of the two wins and the conflict is reported.
%% Note X4: A malformed profile, or an overrides value that is not an object or not one of the guard's tiers, gives that guard's FLOOR
%%    (block, or none for prodDatabase and prodServer). The floor is never off: could-not-tell must not read as opted-out.
